---
description: How to work on the NDW Florida website. Read AGENTS.md before any change.
alwaysApply: true
---

Hard rule: never make a change on your own initiative. Act only when the owner explicitly asks for a specific change, and only within that request. No proactive fixes, refactors, cleanups, dependency or content updates, or "improvements" unless asked. If you notice a problem, you may mention it, but do not change anything until the owner says yes. Every change goes on a branch and a pull request against `main`. Never push straight to `main`. Nothing merges or goes live without the owner's explicit approval.

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root before you change this site. It is the full manual. This rule is the short version.

NDW Florida is the one-page site for Neighborhood Dog Walkers in Melbourne, Florida (https://ndwflorida.com). It is plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. No build step.

GitHub Pages publishes `main` from `/`. `CNAME` is `ndwflorida.com`. `.nojekyll` must stay. Merging to `main` is what goes live. After a merge, reload https://ndwflorida.com and confirm the change.

Always work on a branch and open a pull request against `main`. Never push straight to `main`. The owner confirms before merge.

Keep the visual design. Photos are WebP plus a JPG fallback, lazy-loaded below the fold, each with a real alt or video label. Phone and email live in the contact cards, footer, noscript note, mailto action, and LocalBusiness JSON-LD. Price buttons say "Contact us" and open the call sheet. Keep SEO, Open Graph, JSON-LD, `robots.txt`, and `sitemap.xml` in sync.

The Formspree id is the empty `ndw-formspree-id` meta. Do not invent an id. Empty means the email app, with the phone and email still on the page.

Never rewrite the owner's wording without asking. Still open: "street rat", "scared or aggressive", and group-walk "Varies by how many dogs".

Before a site change is ready: check desktop and mobile, no broken assets, no console errors, and the form and popups work.

Answer the owner in short, simple sentences.

Do not merge or delete `cursor/owner-content-81ff`, `cursor/gallery-no-text-81ff`, or `cursor/custom-domain-81ff` unless the owner asks.
